NAME
       sleep - wait for a number of seconds

SYNOPSIS
       sleep NUMBER[SUFFIX]...

DESCRIPTION
       sleep does nothing for the time given, then exits. Scripts use it to
       wait between two steps. NUMBER may have a decimal point (sleep 0.5).
       The suffix is s for seconds (the default), m for minutes, h for hours or
       d for days. When several times are given, sleep waits for their total.

EXAMPLES
       Wait two seconds, then check a service again:

           sleep 2; systemctl is-active httpd

       Wait one and a half minutes:

           sleep 1m 30s

SEE ALSO
       timeout(1), watch(1)
